{
  "description": "Retry decisions. Each case runs one request against the scripted responses in order: {status, headers?, body?, abortAfter?}, {network: true}, {timeout: true} (the SDK timeout) or {callerTimeout: true} (the signal of the caller times out). request.idempotencyKey is an Idempotency-Key header the caller sets; request.idempotent marks an operation the API deduplicates by that key, as the SDK methods for it do. client and request options default to the SDK defaults; delaysMs bounds each wait in order; error.kind names the error type (see README.md). expected.hookSequence is the order of the hook calls: onRequest before every attempt, onRetry before each retry, onResponse once on the final response (none when the last attempt got no response), then onSuccess on a 2xx or onError; a hook that throws ends it.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "GET 408 is retried",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/emails/em_1"
      },
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 408
        },
        {
          "status": 200
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "calls": 2,
        "delaysMs": [
          [
            375,
            500
          ]
        ],
        "result": {
          "status": 200
        },
        "hookSequence": [
          "onRequest",
          "onRetry",
          "onRequest",
          "onResponse",
          "onSuccess"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
